        "status": "met",
        "evidence": "Everything is on level 0."
      }
    ],
    "summary": "I couldn't fit five drawers in a single hex base. A single base holds one drawer at most, so I built one base with one drawer.\n\n- **Full base:** a drawer can't fit at all. A drawer has to sit on the cut face of a half base.\n- **Half base:** this has one cut face, so it takes exactly one drawer. With that drawer fitted, the configurator offers no more drawer spots.\n- **Quarter base:** I tried this as well and it takes no drawers.\n\nWhat's built: one north-half hex base (piece:0,0,0;half-n) with one classic drawer on its cut face. There are 5 parts in the parts list (the drawer and its hardware count as several), about 507 g of filament. check_build found no errors, and the collision check came back clear.\n\nNormally I'd also add end caps and bolt the joints. I left both out because you asked for nothing to be added to the base. That leaves 3 edges of the base uncapped.\n\nIf you need five drawers, it would take several half bases joined together, which goes against \"a single base\".",
    "outcome": "compromise"
  },
